%% references.bib -- prior-art bibliography for generator-verifier-lean
%%
%% Assembled during the September 2026 literature and provenance audit
%% (see docs/NOVELTY_AND_PROVENANCE.md).
%%
%% Scope note. This repository formalizes the real-algebra skeleton of a
%% capacity/queueing model of multi-agent systems in which "generator" and
%% "verifier" are AGENT ROLES with service rates -- not an untrusted-producer /
%% trusted-checker trust architecture. The bibliography is split accordingly:
%% entries that bear on what is actually formalized (capacity balancing,
%% staffing thresholds, correlated-error averaging), entries for the Lean
%% platform, and a small canon of the trust-architecture literature included
%% precisely to document that this repository is NOT an instance of it.
%%
%% Every entry with a DOI was generated from that DOI's registered metadata
%% (Crossref, or DataCite for the Zenodo deposit) rather than retyped. The two
%% entries without a DOI are monographs and carry a note saying so.

